{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a novel catalytic, enantioselective conjugate amination of alpha,beta-unsaturated 2-acyl imidazoles with N-aryl carbamates. The reaction utilizes a visible-light-induced proton-coupled electron transfer (PCET) mechanism followed by a stereocontrolled radical-radical coupling, mediated by a chiral-at-rhodium Lewis acid catalyst and an iridium photoredox catalyst. This approach achieves high yields and excellent enantioselectivities (up to 99% ee).",
